WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Palantir's potential trillion dollar valuation gives TFSA holders a concrete AI name to screen for volume confirmation before any entry. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 172. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:39.380
real money to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,586, downed 4 tenths of 1%. The NASDAQ composite

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:51.260
finished at 25,982, off 8 tenths of 1%. The TSX composite ended at 35,582, lower by 3 tenths

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:58.740
of 1%. Futures now price at 94% chance the Federal Reserve raises rates this week and a follow-on

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:06.040
move before December. Net breadth narrowed from minus 85 to minus 21, as 53 names beat

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.800
the index while 74 lagged. Breadth readings act as an early filter for whether a market

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.800
move has participation, or is just a narrow handful of names carrying the index. Today's

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.080
flip from negative to less negative breadth on a down day for the S&amp;P shows how sector

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.300
Rotation can produce quick reversals in leadership, even when headline indices finish lower.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:35.500
The S&amp;P itself fell 4800s of 1%, yet the number of stocks beating the index rose from

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:41.700
30 on Friday to 53 on Monday, while Lagerd's fell from 115 to 74.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.260
Investors can track this by comparing the number of stocks above their 20-day average to

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:52.340
those below it, or by watching the advance decline line on the same platform that supplies

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.200
their charts. The approach works best when a single session's bread swing exceeds recent averages,

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.380
as it did Monday, because that signal's capital is rotating rather than exiting.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.540
Risk appears when bread improves but volume stays below the 20-day average, leaving the move

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:15.440
vulnerable to quick reversal. Platforms such as trading view or thinker swim let users overlay

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:21.560
bread indicators directly on index charts for daily checks. Canadian investors can apply the same

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.600
filter inside a TFSA by screening TSX names for the same advanced decline differential

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.400
before committing new capital.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:37.320
About 20 days ago we picked PNG.v which closed down 5.59% after earnings momentum faded

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.540
without volume support.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.420
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.220
No real money is involved.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.220
This is not financial advice.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.820
Today's pick is none, monitoring PLTR on the NASDAQ in the tech sector.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.500
The strategy is catalyst-driven entry on analyst price target upgrade with volume filter,

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:03.120
held for five sessions from entry. Invalidation occurs if PLTR closes

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.160
below its 20-day moving average on volume above the 20-day average,

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.520
at which point the trillion-dollar narrative loses confirmation.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:16.520
Dan Ives' public statement that Palantir could reach a trillion dollar valuation creates

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:21.960
a visible narrative catalyst on the same day multiple desks revise their Fed forecasts higher.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:27.780
No earnings release or contract win accompanied the statement, so the catalyst remains purely

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.460
narrative until volume or price action confirms participation.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:37.400
The stock sits above its 50-day moving average, but requires a volume spike above the 20-day

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.140
average to confirm participation.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:44.100
The current setup shows price holding the intermediate trend while breaded across the

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:50.300
broader market improved, yet relative volume on PLTR itself has not yet exceeded its recent

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:55.900
average. Stop loss sits at the 20-day moving average with maximum acceptable loss capped

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:01.980
at 6-8% given current regime. The cold streak regime check advises raising the bar for

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.780
any new entry, which is why the position remains on watch rather than deployed. Target remains

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.940
means plus 4% to plus 8% over 5 sessions if volume confirms and sector rotation holds.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.920
Confidence sits at medium because the valuation narrative is confirmed by the analyst comment.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.980
Yet sector rotation signals remain mixed and volume confirmation is still pending.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.840
The setup forces an explicit volume gate before entry, directly applying the rule that

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.320
catalyst names already in rotation require volume above the 20-day average.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:40.340
image. Imagine you bought a data center name last week after it posted record quarterly

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:45.380
sales and raised guidance. Your order filled at the open, yet the position is already

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:50.440
down 4% because the broader tech rotation you assumed would support it never arrived.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.360
Without a written invalidation, every dip gets rationalized as noise until the loss grows

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.180
large enough to force an exit that hindsight then labels a mistake.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:05.800
Professionals write the exact observable trigger first, such as if the next two sessions

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:11.120
close below the 50-day moving average on volume above the 20-day average, then set the

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.140
stop at that level.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:18.040
Most retail investors skip this step and later describe the loss only as it went down,

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.600
which prevents learning what actually broke.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.900
The concrete fix is to type the invalidation sentence into the same note where you record

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.220
the entry thesis before the order is placed.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:34.280
This practice converts a loss from an emotional event into a data point about which assumption failed.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.620
It also forces the investor to define success and failure in observable market terms,

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.700
rather than in feelings about the name.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.780
Overrepeated trades, the habit reveals patterns in which types of invalidation trigger most often,

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:52.540
allowing the investor to refine entry criteria before the next position is sized.

